<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="0.16" dur="5.36">Thank you very much everybody.</text><text start="2.8" dur="5.44">Wow.</text><text start="5.52" dur="6.159">You should have seen you should have</text><text start="8.24" dur="5.359">seen the ride in from the airport. Every</text><text start="11.679" dur="5.801">block, every inch, every everything.</text><text start="13.599" dur="3.881">There&amp;#39;s so many people.</text><text start="18.56" dur="6.639">Thousands and thousands and Hello, Ohio.</text><text start="22.96" dur="6.04">You know,</text><text start="25.199" dur="3.801">I love this house.</text><text start="29.279" dur="4.721">People don&amp;#39;t know I worked in Ohio for a</text><text start="31.92" dur="7.44">big beautiful summer when I was a young</text><text start="34" dur="7.2">guy. Cincinnati, Ohio. Sweden village.</text><text start="39.36" dur="4.48">It was a great experience. So, I loved</text><text start="41.2" dur="4.48">it. But I&amp;#39;m thrilled to be back in this</text><text start="43.84" dur="6.64">beautiful state which I won all three</text><text start="45.68" dur="7.96">times with the most votes ever gotten.</text><text start="50.48" dur="3.16">Not even</text><text start="55.199" dur="5.2">I even beat Bernie Marino. But John</text><text start="58.48" dur="4.559">Houston&amp;#39;s going to beat me in Vake. I</text><text start="60.399" dur="4.16">hope you beat me, too. I don&amp;#39;t I&amp;#39;m not</text><text start="63.039" dur="5.16">proud.</text><text start="64.559" dur="3.64">I&amp;#39;m not proud.</text><text start="73.439" dur="6.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Boy, oh boy. Since I explained to people</text><text start="76.799" dur="5.121">that he was a phenomenal, not a good a</text><text start="80.159" dur="3.841">phenomenal football player, you have</text><text start="81.92" dur="4.32">really taken on new life. You are</text><text start="84" dur="3.52">something.</text><text start="86.24" dur="3.519">You know, I always thought of him as</text><text start="87.52" dur="5.12">this really solid guy. He&amp;#39;s a solid</text><text start="89.759" dur="4.72">rock. But I didn&amp;#39;t see this. And it was</text><text start="92.64" dur="3.28">actually John Gruden, the great coach,</text><text start="94.479" dur="3.6">great coach, and I guess a very good</text><text start="95.92" dur="3.839">quarterback, right? But he was a great</text><text start="98.079" dur="3.841">coach and is a great coach. And he</text><text start="99.759" dur="4.801">explained to me. He said, &amp;quot;No, I&amp;#39;m here</text><text start="101.92" dur="4.08">to see my I&amp;#39;m here to see my teammate.</text><text start="104.56" dur="3.28">Who the hell is your teammate, John?&amp;quot;</text><text start="106" dur="3.439">Because I saw him a couple of weeks ago</text><text start="107.84" dur="3.76">at the rally. We had a big rally,</text><text start="109.439" dur="4.64">another one. And I said, &amp;quot;Who&amp;#39;s your</text><text start="111.6" dur="5.12">teammate?&amp;quot; He said, &amp;quot;John,&amp;quot; you said,</text><text start="114.079" dur="5.841">&amp;quot;Oh, I didn&amp;#39;t know he played football.&amp;quot;</text><text start="116.72" dur="5.039">And then he said, &amp;quot;No, he was great. We</text><text start="119.92" dur="3.36">had the championship team. We won the</text><text start="121.759" dur="3.68">championship. He was the best player in</text><text start="123.28" dur="3.92">the team. He was the fastest player. He</text><text start="125.439" dur="4.16">was an all-American.&amp;quot; And the thing that</text><text start="127.2" dur="5.84">really impressed me, he said, and when</text><text start="129.599" dur="6.441">he tackled people, he&amp;#39;d rip their heads</text><text start="133.04" dur="3">off.</text><text start="136.56" dur="3.6">And I&amp;#39;ve known Jo, you know, he&amp;#39;s been</text><text start="138.16" dur="3.52">my friend for a long time.</text><text start="140.16" dur="2.799">You know, see, if I were him, I would</text><text start="141.68" dur="4.08">have said I was one of the greatest</text><text start="142.959" dur="5.28">players ever to come out of Ohio.</text><text start="145.76" dur="4.32">He doesn&amp;#39;t do that. He&amp;#39;s a humble guy.</text><text start="148.239" dur="4.481">So, he didn&amp;#39;t talk about it. It took</text><text start="150.08" dur="5.36">John took a great coach to brag about</text><text start="152.72" dur="4.64">you. And I thought it was great. And</text><text start="155.44" dur="4.72">then I got myself in trouble because</text><text start="157.36" dur="6">after after they told me that damn</text><text start="160.16" dur="5.12">story, I got myself in big trouble</text><text start="163.36" dur="3.92">because I always ask somebody to come up</text><text start="165.28" dur="4.16">and say a few words, right? Say a few</text><text start="167.28" dur="4.16">words. And</text><text start="169.44" dur="3.6">I said, &amp;quot;John, come come on up.&amp;quot; But</text><text start="171.44" dur="3.68">John Gruden just told me about his</text><text start="173.04" dur="4.559">football pro. They won the championship,</text><text start="175.12" dur="5.96">by the way, the whole championship. And</text><text start="177.599" dur="3.481">he was the best.</text><text start="183.28" dur="5.76">And he set the NCAA record. He&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="186" dur="6.879">safety for interception 17. I said, &amp;quot;You</text><text start="189.04" dur="5.839">got to be kidding, this guy.&amp;quot; And I</text><text start="192.879" dur="4.801">looked at him sort of like, you know,</text><text start="194.879" dur="4.241">he&amp;#39;s always dressed up and nice and he</text><text start="197.68" dur="4.32">was a great lieutenant governor, but</text><text start="199.12" dur="5.52">low-key, very low-key, man. But he was</text><text start="202" dur="6.08">the guy. But I looked at him as being a</text><text start="204.64" dur="5.44">very high quality, nice man that if I</text><text start="208.08" dur="4.96">got into a fight with him, I&amp;#39;d rip his</text><text start="210.08" dur="4.239">heart out.</text><text start="213.04" dur="3.36">And it would have been just the</text><text start="214.319" dur="3.84">opposite. It would this would not That&amp;#39;s</text><text start="216.4" dur="3.52">the kind of guy, you know, you say,</text><text start="218.159" dur="4.241">&amp;quot;Come on, let&amp;#39;s go at it.&amp;quot; And then it</text><text start="219.92" dur="5.76">doesn&amp;#39;t end well for you, right, John?</text><text start="222.4" dur="4.559">So he came up and he said a few words. I</text><text start="225.68" dur="5.6">said, &amp;quot;John, say hello.&amp;quot; We had a</text><text start="226.959" dur="7.441">tremendous crowd. And then I got up and</text><text start="231.28" dur="5.44">I made this terrible mistake. So you</text><text start="234.4" dur="5.72">know the way they speak and I&amp;#39;ll stand</text><text start="236.72" dur="3.4">usually over.</text><text start="277.28" dur="4.359">USA us</text><text start="290.479" dur="6.401">Oh, these people. You know, there&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="293.919" dur="4.641">guy, not a young guy. They gave him</text><text start="296.88" dur="3.599">$250.</text><text start="298.56" dur="5.32">Paid protesters.</text><text start="300.479" dur="3.401">Paid protesters.</text><text start="311.6" dur="4.96">USA. USA. USA.</text><text start="331.039" dur="6.361">Such such losers. Boy, you look at that</text><text start="334.4" dur="3">guy.</text><text start="338.32" dur="5.28">So that guy, he&amp;#39;s right out of the</text><text start="340.88" dur="5.84">radical left playbook. He&amp;#39;s right out of</text><text start="343.6" dur="5.599">the rad. This guy, this guy was very</text><text start="346.72" dur="5.68">nondescript, but I will say this, you</text><text start="349.199" dur="5.28">know, he mentioned Epstein. So, I threw</text><text start="352.4" dur="4.56">Jeffrey Epstein out of a club like 20</text><text start="354.479" dur="5.801">years ago because I thought he was a</text><text start="356.96" dur="3.32">black child.</text><text start="361.28" dur="5.039">That was a great, by the way, that was</text><text start="364.08" dur="4">the great thing I did, I must tell you.</text><text start="366.319" dur="4">And he never came up with me. You know</text><text start="368.08" dur="4.88">who he came up with? All of the friends</text><text start="370.319" dur="4.961">of the Democrats. He was a Democrat. He</text><text start="372.96" dur="4.079">had all friends. And whenever they bring</text><text start="375.28" dur="4.16">his name, you know, like the guy who is</text><text start="377.039" dur="3.841">the head of Harvard who can&amp;#39;t, you got</text><text start="379.44" dur="4.16">thrown off the board and all his</text><text start="380.88" dur="6.759">friends. No, I threw Jeffrey Epstein the</text><text start="383.6" dur="4.039">hell out of Mara Lago</text><text start="393.12" dur="4.48">and I was the one that was totally</text><text start="394.8" dur="5.839">exonerated from him. But you know, they</text><text start="397.6" dur="5.599">use it because that&amp;#39;s what they do.</text><text start="400.639" dur="5.12">They&amp;#39;re sick, weak people. And these</text><text start="403.199" dur="5.361">guys are paid protesters. Think of a</text><text start="405.759" dur="5.761">guy, that guy&amp;#39;s probably 45, 50 years</text><text start="408.56" dur="4.96">old. They give him $250. We have a trace</text><text start="411.52" dur="4.32">down, $250.</text><text start="413.52" dur="5.76">And he screws up his life. And now he</text><text start="415.84" dur="6.68">goes home and his boyfriend gets upset</text><text start="419.28" dur="3.24">with him.</text><text start="430.88" dur="3">USA.</text><text start="434.639" dur="3">USA.</text><text start="447.12" dur="4.24">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No,</text><text start="449.36" dur="4.88">they&amp;#39;re professional protesters. They</text><text start="451.36" dur="6.08">get money. They get money. We have them</text><text start="454.24" dur="6.16">all the time. And you know what happens</text><text start="457.44" dur="4.72">is their poll numbers just keep going up</text><text start="460.4" dur="5.12">when that happens because everybody gets</text><text start="462.16" dur="5.2">it. They get paid $250. They then get</text><text start="465.52" dur="4.64">booked and they screw up their whole</text><text start="467.36" dur="4.16">lives. It&amp;#39;s a crazy thing. It&amp;#39;s a crazy</text><text start="470.16" dur="4.4">thing.</text><text start="471.52" dur="5.519">So, I was about to tell you a story and</text><text start="474.56" dur="5.88">they always hit me right in the middle</text><text start="477.039" dur="3.401">of the punchline</text><text start="481.52" dur="5.84">because I was about to say that I was</text><text start="483.919" dur="6.96">examining that man for his physical</text><text start="487.36" dur="5.44">proess and I got it. When he stood up, I</text><text start="490.879" dur="3.681">looked at him. I looked him all over the</text><text start="492.8" dur="4.64">place and I should have never said what</text><text start="494.56" dur="7.639">I said, but I said I started by looking</text><text start="497.44" dur="4.759">at his ass and it was strong as hell.</text><text start="502.479" dur="6.201">And the problem is the fake news. Look</text><text start="504.479" dur="4.201">at all that fake news back there.</text><text start="512" dur="5.519">The fake news.</text><text start="514.24" dur="5.44">They didn&amp;#39;t wait for this. They said, &amp;quot;I</text><text start="517.519" dur="4.96">looked at his ass and they cut.&amp;quot; And</text><text start="519.68" dur="4.56">then they all night LONG THEY SAY, &amp;quot;WHY</text><text start="522.479" dur="5.121">DID HE SAY THAT?&amp;quot; IN OTHER WORDS, THEY</text><text start="524.24" dur="6.56">just went cut. And it didn&amp;#39;t look good</text><text start="527.6" dur="6.64">for me. Now, now fortunately, it was</text><text start="530.8" dur="5.68">only 5% of them, but 5%&amp;#39;s a lot.</text><text start="534.24" dur="5.2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; When when you don&amp;#39;t like those things,</text><text start="536.48" dur="5.68">5%. No, but I did I looked I looked at</text><text start="539.44" dur="5.04">John. I studied his physique because I</text><text start="542.16" dur="4">wanted to find out that man who I&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="544.48" dur="4.72">known for a long time, who&amp;#39;s one of the</text><text start="546.16" dur="4.96">most respected people, I would say, in</text><text start="549.2" dur="4.48">the country in Washington. Everybody</text><text start="551.12" dur="5.36">respects him. But I didn&amp;#39;t see him as a</text><text start="553.68" dur="6">physical person. And when John Guden</text><text start="556.48" dur="6.72">said he rips their heads off when he</text><text start="559.68" dur="5.76">tackles in in football, that&amp;#39;s a coach&amp;#39;s</text><text start="563.2" dur="5.04">dream. He said he was the best player on</text><text start="565.44" dur="5.12">the team. So I did. I studied him. Not</text><text start="568.24" dur="5.039">only what I just said, I studied the</text><text start="570.56" dur="4.399">feet, the legs, the shoulders. I tapped</text><text start="573.279" dur="5.361">him on the shoulder and it was like a</text><text start="574.959" dur="6.161">piece was like my hand was like hitting</text><text start="578.64" dur="4.879">a piece of steel and he took on a whole</text><text start="581.12" dur="5.12">I explained this and he took on a whole</text><text start="583.519" dur="6.241">new persona. He went from sort of like</text><text start="586.24" dur="7.52">Clark Kent if you think about it and he</text><text start="589.76" dur="7.24">became Superman and a number of</text><text 