4.08">me see. I saw him the other day. He was</text><text start="1035.52" dur="3.919">trying to explain why he&amp;#39;s opposed to</text><text start="1037.039" dur="5.121">voter ID. You know why he said? He said</text><text start="1039.439" dur="4.64">in the end, I don&amp;#39;t know.</text><text start="1042.16" dur="4.72">Could I answer? Guy&amp;#39;s only been doing</text><text start="1044.079" dur="5.761">this for 53 years. Couldn&amp;#39;t answer the</text><text start="1046.88" dur="4.88">question. But he backstabbed Ohio. You</text><text start="1049.84" dur="5.44">know, until I came around, Ohio was not</text><text start="1051.76" dur="6.08">a successful state. We really turned</text><text start="1055.28" dur="5.92">things around in 2016. Which was a</text><text start="1057.84" dur="6.32">bigger election, 2016 or 2024? And by</text><text start="1061.2" dur="6.96">the way, we won in 2022, but let&amp;#39;s we</text><text start="1064.16" dur="6.96">won in 2020 also.</text><text start="1068.16" dur="7.2">We won in 20</text><text start="1071.12" dur="7.28">we had we won three times,</text><text start="1075.36" dur="6.24">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; but in 2020</text><text start="1078.4" dur="5.04">in 2020 it was a rigged election</text><text start="1081.6" dur="4.4">and we have to stop that. That&amp;#39;s why we</text><text start="1083.44" dur="5.68">want Save America and all that. But</text><text start="1086" dur="5.12">Sherid Brown voted for every single</text><text start="1089.12" dur="4.799">Democrat bill that gave you the worst</text><text start="1091.12" dur="4.88">inflation in American history, the</text><text start="1093.919" dur="4.64">highest energy prices in American</text><text start="1096" dur="4.64">history, the worst trade deficit in</text><text start="1098.559" dur="3.681">American history, and totally open</text><text start="1100.64" dur="4.8">borders. How about the open borders?</text><text start="1102.24" dur="8">With 25 million illegal aliens pouring</te