ody leans left, I have no idea. I&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="1183.039" dur="4.241">never But he was leaning left and he</text><text start="1185.2" dur="4.4">didn&amp;#39;t understand it either. Under</text><text start="1187.28" dur="5.44">Sharon Brown, Ohio lost more than</text><text start="1189.6" dur="5.76">300,000 manufacturing jobs. I watched</text><text start="1192.72" dur="4.56">it. I used to talk. I wasn&amp;#39;t in politics</text><text start="1195.36" dur="4">at that point. Who the hell I have not</text><text start="1197.28" dur="3.84">been doing? I&amp;#39;ll tell you what, to</text><text start="1199.36" dur="4.08">become a three-time winner of the</text><text start="1201.12" dur="6.28">presidency, I have not been doing this</text><text start="1203.44" dur="3.96">very long. Let&amp;#39;s face,</text><text start="1208.4" dur="5.48">you know, 10 years, not</text><text start="1214.88" dur="3.44">doing great. I had the greatest</text><text start="1216.48" dur="4.079">television show, but I had a great</text><text start="1218.32" dur="3.599">company. I was really good at real</text><text start="1220.559" dur="4.161">estate. You know, I get criticized</text><text start="1221.919" dur="5.12">because the White House has to be</text><text start="1224.72" dur="5.199">beautiful outside, right? It has to need</text><text start="1227.039" dur="6.481">that exterior plaster. The bricks were</text><text start="1229.919" dur="6.401">fallen. The stone was broken. The</text><text start="1233.52" dur="6.32">monuments were coming off. The the</text><text start="1236.32" dur="6.479">beautiful windows were cracked. It</text><text start="1239.84" dur="6.079">looked terrible. And I fixed it very</text><text start="1242.799" dur="6.481">inexpensively. I paid for it myself. I</text><text start="1245.919" dur="4.721">fixed it. And</text><text start="1249.28" dur="3.36">now</text><text start="1250.64" dur="3.36">And now it&amp;#39;s more beautiful and in</text><text start="1252.64" dur="2.72">better shape. You know, you&amp;#39;d have a</text><text start="1254" dur="3.919">window and have a what they call a</text><text start="1255.36" dur="4.319">monument. They would have a beautiful</text><text start="1257.919" dur="4.401">stone on one side, the other side it was</text><text start="1259.679" dur="5.601">half broken and falling probably 25</text><text start="1262.32" dur="5.599">years ago. And I noticed those things. I</text><text start="1265.28" dur="5.68">came to the vi White House 20 years ago.</text><text start="1267.919" dur="5.201">I said to I don&amp;#39;t know maybe like a</text><text start="1270.96" dur="5.12">fundraiser for a president, another</text><text start="1273.12" dur="5.439">beautiful president. And I said, &amp;quot;This</text><text start="1276.08" dur="4.16">place is in bad shape, man.&amp;quot; And I</text><text start="1278.559" dur="5.561">decided to make it beautiful and</text><text start="1280.24" dur="3.88">pristine. And I did.</text><text start="1289.2" dur="4.88">And you know, some of the uh stone on</text><text start="1292.08" dur="3.839">the outside was badly broken from a</text><text start="1294.08" dur="3.12">truck that hit it 30 years ago and it</text><text start="1295.919" dur="4.321">never got finished. You know, you&amp;#39;d have</text><text start="1297.2" dur="5.44">a big chunk of stone at the entrances.</text><text start="1300.24" dur="6.08">There was one piece of stone. It drove</text><text start="1302.64" dur="5.84">me. I&amp;#39;d walk out and I&amp;#39;d see this stone</text><text start="1306.32" dur="5.28">and it was just like a big hole in the</text><text start="1308.48" dur="5.439">wall and we fix it all. It&amp;#39;s beautiful,</text><text start="1311.6" dur="4.4">beautiful exterior plaster. It&amp;#39;s so</text><text start="1313.919" dur="5.841">beautiful. Hasn&amp;#39;t been that way since</text><text start="1316" dur="8.84">1792. Better than it was in 17. and</text><text start="1319.76" dur="5.08">President Obama who doesn&amp;#39;t understand</text><text start="1326.96" dur="4.4">who doesn&amp;#39;t understand cleanliness who</text><text start="1329.2" dur="3.76">doesn&amp;#39;t understand</text><text start="1331.36" dur="5.04">broken</text><text start="1332.96" dur="6.079">cracked stone and sidewalk who doesn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="1336.4" dur="4.48">understand that having asphalt going to</text><text start="1339.039" dur="4.561">your main entrance is not the right</text><text start="1340.88" dur="5.2">thing. We&amp;#39;d like to have granates and</text><text start="1343.6" dur="5.199">marbles. We&amp;#39;d like to have it look nice.</text><text start="1346.08" dur="6.719">You don&amp;#39;t use asphalt. Use asphalt for a</text><text start="1348.799" dur="6.641">street. Use asphalt to patch to patch up</text><text start="1352.799" dur="4.721">your streets, but you don&amp;#39;t use asphalt</text><text start="1355.44" dur="4.64">to go into the White House. Anyway, we</text><text start="1357.52" dur="6.08">made it unbelievable. And I took heat</text><text start="1360.08" dur="5.28">because Obama, who is I mean, I always</text><text start="1363.6" dur="4.16">worry when he campaigns against me</text><text start="1365.36" dur="6.92">because he got involved with Hillary</text><text start="1367.76" dur="4.52">Clinton. He was really Oh,</text><text start="1372.799" dur="5.041">and he lost. He then got involved with</text><text start="1376.159" dur="3.681">Kamala</text><text start="1377.84" dur="5.199">and he lost</text><text start="1379.84" dur="5.68">and he lost. They said Obama&amp;#39;s coming. I</text><text start="1383.039" dur="5.76">said that&amp;#39;s good because you know but no</text><text start="1385.52" dur="5.519">he he took HE SAID WHY IS HE SPENDING SO</text><text start="1388.799" dur="4.641">MUCH time fixing up the WHITE HOUSE? WHY</text><text start="1391.039" dur="4.64">IS HE doing that? You know why? Because</text><text start="1393.44" dur="5.04">the White House I think is the number</text><text start="1395.679" dur="6.161">one symbol of our country. And we can&amp;#39;t</text><text start="1398.48" dur="6.079">have a White House with broken windows,</text><text start="1401.84" dur="6.079">with broken stone that hasn&amp;#39;t been</text><text start="1404.559" dur="7.6">painted in 30 years. And now the other</text><text start="1407.919" dur="6.64">day I left I left. Where did I leave?</text><text start="1412.159" dur="4.481">Mississippi. And I was coming home very</text><text start="1414.559" dur="4.081">late. I got home very late. I&amp;#39;ve been</text><text start="1416.64" dur="4.72">getting home late every single night. My</text><text start="1418.64" dur="6.08">wife thinks I&amp;#39;m crazy.</text><text start="1421.36" dur="4.88">And we were riding up that drive and the</text><text start="1424.72" dur="4.48">lights were on. You know, the lights</text><text start="1426.24" dur="4.96">were different colors. Before they&amp;#39;d</text><text start="1429.2" dur="4.08">have a light one, a little darker one,</text><text start="1431.2" dur="4.959">another light one, now one that was</text><text start="1433.28" dur="5.279">broken. It was terrible. And now they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="1436.159" dur="4.321">magnificent light. All the best you can</text><text start="1438.559" dur="3.841">get. The exterior lighting is so</text><text start="1440.48" dur="3.52">beautiful.</text><text start="1442.4" dur="5.12">And</text><text start="1444" dur="6.4">and I was driving up and I said, &amp;quot;Does</text><text start="1447.52" dur="5.36">that look beautiful?&amp;quot; So I just say</text><text start="1450.4" dur="5.12">that, you know, I do it out of my back</text><text start="1452.88" dur="4.24">pocket. I fix it and I do it naturally.</text><text start="1455.52" dur="4.08">In fact, for me, it relax for some</text><text start="1457.12" dur="4.32">people that kind of thing is, you know,</text><text start="145