gle Democrat in Congress voted</text><text start="4490.719" dur="5.121">against our tax cuts. Every single</text><text start="4493.84" dur="5.52">Democrat, every single one, I think,</text><text start="4495.84" dur="6.16">Bernie, right? They voted against no tax</text><text start="4499.36" dur="5.52">and tips. They voted against no tax on</text><text start="4502" dur="5.28">overtime. They voted against no tax on</text><text start="4504.88" dur="5.04">social security for our seniors. They</text><text start="4507.28" dur="5.12">voted against voter ID because they want</text><text start="4509.92" dur="4.64">to cheat. They voted against proof of</text><text start="4512.4" dur="4.48">citizenship because they want to cheat.</text><text start="4514.56" dur="4.639">They voted against securing the border.</text><text start="4516.88" dur="4.4">They wanted open borders. They voted in</text><text start="4519.199" dur="4.641">favor of the worst inflation and highest</text><text start="4521.28" dur="5.76">energy cost in American history. In</text><text start="4523.84" dur="6.319">favor of the transgender utilization of</text><text start="4527.04" dur="5.52">your children, in favor of men and women</text><text start="4530.159" dur="3.921">sports and they want to take away your</text><text start="4532.56" dur="4.8">guns. Other than that, they&amp;#39;re quite</text><text start="4534.08" dur="5.84">good. I think quite good. On election</text><text start="4537.36" dur="4.799">night in Ohio, you&amp;#39;re going to approve</text><text start="4539.92" dur="4.88">that America does not belong to those</text><text start="4542.159" dur="6.921">who hate it. America belongs to those</text><text start="4544.8" dur="4.28">like you who love it.</text><text start="4553.92" dur="4.96">So to me, this is one of the most</text><text start="4556.64" dur="5.12">important elections. You have a</text><text start="4558.88" dur="6.08">tremendous man as your representative,</text><text start="4561.76" dur="6.32">as your senator, respected by everybody</text><text start="4564.96" dur="4.56">so much for many, many reasons. I didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="4568.08" dur="3.28">know he was a great athlete, but now</text><text start="4569.52" dur="4.96">I&amp;#39;ll add that to him. But it&amp;#39;s less</text><text start="4571.36" dur="4.799">important in many ways. But being great</text><text start="4574.48" dur="4">at something, whether it&amp;#39;s in sports or</text><text start="4576.159" dur="4">anything, means something, but it&amp;#39;s less</text><text start="4578.48" dur="3.52">important than his other qualities. His</text><text start="4580.159" dur="3.52">qualities are incredible. He&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="4582" dur="4.88">brilliant guy. He&amp;#39;s a great guy. He&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="4583.679" dur="7.641">humble man. and he loves your state.</text><text start="4586.88" dur="4.44">John Houston, please come up.</text><text start="4600.64" dur="4.32">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you, Mr. President, for caring</text><text start="4602.48" dur="4.48">about Ohio and coming back again and</text><text start="4604.96" dur="6.36">again and again to help us win this</text><text start="4606.96" dur="4.36">election on Tuesday. Is that right?</text><text start="4615.04" dur="4.4">I have to tell a story about the</text><text start="4616.88" dur="4.48">president because one day I I got a call</text><text start="4619.44" dur="4.88">from the president and the plant manager</text><text start="4621.36" dur="5.6">from Kenworth and they said, &amp;quot;Hey, our</text><text start="4624.32" dur="5.359">plant&amp;#39;s in trouble.&amp;quot; They said, &amp;quot;We need</text><text start="4626.96" dur="6">a fair trade deal. Foreign companies are</text><text start="4629.679" dur="7.601">assembling trucks in Mexico, avoiding</text><text start="4632.96" dur="6.719">the costs and undermining our plant here</text><text start="4637.28" dur="5.04">in Chilikathy. and if we don&amp;#39;t get a</text><text start="4639.679" dur="4.56">good trade deal, our plant&amp;#39;s going to</text><text start="4642.32" dur="4.16">have to close and all of those jobs will</text><text start="4644.239" dur="4.081">go away. They said, &amp;quot;Can we come see you</text><text start="4646.48" dur="3.6">and can we talk to you quickly?&amp;quot; I said,</text><text start="4648.32" dur="4.32">&amp;quot;Sure, let&amp;#39;s go have a conversation.</text><text start="4650.08" dur="4.48">Let&amp;#39;s get this done. I want to know.&amp;quot;</text><text start="4652.64" dur="3.92">And so they told me about their plight</text><text start="4654.56" dur="4.4">and I called the president and I called</text><text start="4656.56" dur="4.639">his team and I explained to them that</text><text start="4658.96" dur="5.279">this plant in Chilikathi, one of the</text><text start="4661.199" dur="6.161">great iconic brands in our nation,</text><text start="4664.239" dur="5.92">Kenworth had the was in jeopardy of</text><text start="4667.36" dur="4.24">going under if we didn&amp;#39;t get them a fair</text><text start="4670.159" dur="3.681">trade deal from people who were trying</text><text start="4671.6" dur="4.88">to undermine it. And immediately the</text><text start="4673.84" dur="4.72">president and his team took action,</text><text start="4676.48" dur="6.04">saved the plant and added a thousand</text><text start="4678.56" dur="3.96">jobs right here in Chilikothy.</text><text start="4691.76" dur="3.6">And this is a this is a great thing to</text><text start="4693.6" dur="3.119">remember. When Barack Obama was</text><text start="4695.36" dur="3.44">president, he said, &amp;quot;All of those</text><text start="4696.719" dur="4.801">manufacturing jobs are going to go away.</text><text start="4698.8" dur="5.6">Let&amp;#39;s get used to it.&amp;quot; Since Donald</text><text start="4701.52" dur="5.44">Trump has been president, in the last 20</text><text start="4704.4" dur="6.6">months, we&amp;#39;ve added 10,000 manufacturing</text><text start="4706.96" dur="4.04">jobs right here in Ohio.</text><text start="4717.44" dur="4.239">Mr. President, you have not let Ohio</text><text start="4719.679" dur="5.04">down. Ohio will not let you down. We</text><text start="4721.679" dur="6.681">will win on Tuesday, won&amp;#39;t we, FOLKS?</text><text start="4724.719" dur="3.641">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; LET&amp;#39;S GO GET THEM.</text><text start="4736.32" dur="4.08">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; This guy&amp;#39;s a great guy. Get out and</text><text start="4738.48" dur="5.04">vote. You got to get out and vote. We</text><text start="4740.4" dur="6.16">can&amp;#39;t we can&amp;#39;t take chances. We also</text><text start="4743.52" dur="4.639">need to elect your next governor D</text><text start="4746.56" dur="4.32">Rabiswami</text><text start="4748.159" dur="6.641">running against Amy</text><text start="4750.88" dur="5.839">and she wants to double your taxes.</text><text start="4754.8" dur="4.16">You know, she compares law enforcement</text><text start="4756.719" dur="4.401">to white supremacists. That&amp;#39;s what she</text><text start="4758.96" dur="3.68">said. And she&amp;#39;ll be a disaster in every</text><text start="4761.12" dur="3.68">way aside from the fact that she</text><text start="4762.64" dur="4.72">absolutely wants to take your guns away.</text><text start="4764.8" dur="5.359">We can&amp;#39;t have her be elected. Fake,</text><text start="4767.36" dur="2.799">please come up.</text><text start="4778.08" dur="3.92">Thank you, Mr. President.</text><text start="4780.48" dur="3.759">This election actually comes down to</text><text start="4782" dur="5.28">something very simple. Same thing as the</text><text start="4784.239" dur="4.321">2024 election.</text><text start="4787.28" dur="4">Who&amp;#39;s actually going to make your life</text><text start="4788.56" dur="4.159">better? And if you think about that just</text><text start="4791.28" dur="2.72">honestly, not even the people who are in</text><text start="4792.719" dur="3.921">this room, even the independents</text><text start="4794" dur="6.64">watching at home, who do you actually</text><text start="4796.64" dur="8.079">think is going to make your life better?</text><text start="4800.64" dur="5.84">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; The answer is so clear. In 2024, Donald</text><text start="4804.719" dur="4.081">Trump, you voted for him to do that. You</text><text start="4806.48" dur="4.8">know what he did? He passed the biggest</text><text start="4808.8" dur="5.28">tax relief package we&amp;#39;ve ever seen in</text><text start="4811.28" dur="6.04">our history. And I&amp;#39;m proud of that for</text><text start="4814.08" dur="3.24">our country.</text><text start="4818.239" dur="3.281">And you know what? What I&amp;#39;m going to do</text><text start="4819.36" dur="4.72">after I&amp;#39;m elected, I&amp;#39;m going to pass the</text><text start="4821.52" dur="7.48">biggest property tax relief package Ohio</text><text start="4824.08" dur="4.92">has ever seen in our history.</text><text start="4833.6" dur="3.68">Who&amp;#39;s going to make your life better?</text><text start="4834.96" dur="4.48">President Trump sealed the border to</text><text start="4837.28" dur="6.04">keep illegal immigrants out of the</text><text start="4839.44" dur="3.88">United States of America.</text><text start="4845.679" dur="3.441">And when I&amp;#39;m your next governor, we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="4847.36" dur="3.359">going to end the sanctuary cities to</text><text start="4849.12" dur="4">keep illegal immigrants out of the state</text><text start="4850.719" dur="5.96">of Ohio.</text><text start="4853.12" dur="3.559">It&amp;#39;s that simple.</text><text start="4858.8" dur="4.72">We could go on all night, but it comes</text><text start="4860.48" dur="5.92">down to a very simple premise. President</text><text start="4863.52" dur="5.36">Trump puts Americans first. I&amp;#39;m going to</text><text start="4866.4" dur="4.16">put Ohioans first. We&amp;#39;re going to fight</text><text start="4868.88" dur="3.92">for you and we&amp;#39;re going to win this</text><text start="4870.56" dur="4.639">election next Tuesday night. God bless</text><text start="4872.8" dur="4.399">you and your families. Get out and vote.</text><text start="4875.199" dur="4.401">Let&amp;#39;s get the job done. And we&amp;#39;re taking</text><text start="4877.199" dur="5.96">America and Ohio to the next level.</text><text start="4879.6" dur="3.559">Thank you, Mr. President.</text><text start="4889.679" dur="5.681">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you, fellas. Two great people. I</text><text start="4893.44" dur="4.16">want to also thank my friend, Senator</text><text start="4895.36" dur="5.24">Bernie Marino. You&amp;#39;ve been a fantastic</text><text start="4897.6" dur="3">senator.</text><text start="4902.56" dur="6.159">and Representative Dave Taylor. Thank</text><text start="4905.199" dur="6.241">you, Dave. Great job.</text><text start="4908.719" dur="5.361">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Fantastic man.</text><text start="4911.44" dur="5.92">Nominee for Attorney General, Keith</text><text start="4914.08" dur="5.76">Faber. Keith, thank you. Going to win. I</text><text start="4917.36" dur="5.839">hear you&amp;#39;re doing good.</text><text start="4919.84" dur="6.359">Nominee for Secretary of State, Robert</text><text start="4923.199" dur="3">Sprag.</text><text start="4927.04" dur="6.199">nominee for state treasurer, Jay</text><text start="4929.04" dur="4.199">Edwards. Thank you, Jay.</text><text start="4940.159" dur="4.721">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Nominee for state auditor, a friend of</text><text start="4942" dur="5.679">mine, Frank LaRose. Thank you. Thank</text><text start="4944.88" dur="5.04">you.</text><text start="4947.679" dur="4.721">And a special envoy who&amp;#39;s done a</text><text start="4949.92" dur="5.04">phenomenal job, Mr. Steve Witco. He&amp;#39;s</text><text start="4952.4" dur="5.759">here someplace. Thank you, Steve. Thank</text><text start="4954.96" dur="5.36">you, sir.</text><text start="4958.159" dur="5.841">And the great Dan Scavino, of course, is</text><text start="4960.32" dur="6.64">here. And very important Dan is uh a</text><text start="4964" dur="4.639">person that&amp;#39;s with you, deputy from</text><text start="4966.96" dur="4.56">Mary&amp;#39;sville, Ohio. Do you know</text><text start="4968.639" dur="5.52">Mary&amp;#39;sville, Ohio, anyone?</text><text start="4971.52" dur="4.4">Her name is Morgan Dit and she is</text><text start="4974.159" dur="4.56">phenomenal. She works with us in the</text><text start="4975.92" dur="6.52">office. Thank you, Morgan.</text><text start="4978.719" dur="3.721">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you very much.</text><text start="4982.639" dur="4.721">Thank you, Dad. Another great friend of</text><text start="4985.36" dur="6.96">mine, co-chair. He was with me in Ohio</text><text start="4987.36" dur="9.04">from day one. Bob Pedek. Bob, where are</text><text start="4992.32" dur="5.919">you, Bob? What a great What a great guy.</text><text start="4996.4" dur="4.4">And we have one of the world&amp;#39;s greatest</text><text start="4998.239" dur="5.841">fighters, UFC fighters, Hall of Famer,</text><text start="5000.8" dur="6.56">Rich Franklin. Where is Rich? Thank you,</text><text start="5004.08" dur="5.28">Rich. That guy,</text><text start="5007.36" dur="4.56">I&amp;#39;ve seen you fight. We&amp;#39;re not going to</text><text start="5009.36" dur="5.44">fight you. Great job. Thank you. Congrat</text><text start="5011.92" dur="6.239">Hall of Fame. Hall of Fame. Fantastic.</text><text start="5014.8" dur="5.12">Lot of fights, a lot of wins. Everyone</text><text start="5018.159" dur="3.441">here today is part of the greatest</text><text start="5019.92" dur="3.92">movement in the history of our country.</text><text start="5021.6" dur="3.92">And our spirit is stronger than it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="5023.84" dur="3.76">ever been before. We have the greatest</text><text start="5025.52" dur="4.719">spirit. There&amp;#39;s never been a movement</text><text start="5027.6" dur="4.32">like this. Uh before closing up, I&amp;#39;d</text><text start="5030.239" dur="4.641">like to just show you a couple of charts</text><text start="5031.92" dur="5.2">that CNN produced and you find them very</text><text start="5034.88" dur="5.52">interesting.</text><text start="5037.12" dur="6.079">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Okay. MAGA GOP on Trump. In the 2024</text><text start="5040.4" dur="4.96">election versus Kla Harris, he got 99%</text><text start="5043.199" dur="3.52">of the MAGA GOP vote. Perhaps</text><text start="5045.36" dur="4.24">surprisingly, I might have thought it&amp;#39;d</text><text start="5046.719" dur="4.241">be 100%, but it was 99%.</text><text start="5049.6" dur="4.559">Compare that to his approval rating.</text><text start="5050.96" dur="5.84">Now, at the MAGA GOP, it&amp;#39;s 98%. That is,</text><text start="5054.159" dur="4.401">there&amp;#39;s been no real decline in MAGA</text><text start="5056.8" dur="3.04">support. These folks say that they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="5058.56" dur="3.52">going to vote for congressional</text><text start="5059.84" dur="4.72">Republicans come the midterm elections.</text><text start="5062.08" dur="4.639">Again, that&amp;#39;s the 99% that Trump got</text><text start="5064.56" dur="4.48">against Kla Harris. Look, now in terms</text><text start="5066.719" dur="3.761">of the congressional vote, 98% of them</text><text start="5069.04" dur="3.52">say they&amp;#39;re going to be voting for House</text><text start="5070.48" dur="4.4">Republican candidates. So that support</text><text start="5072.56" dur="4.56">is actually really holding up strong.</text><text start="5074.88" dur="4.799">It&amp;#39;s really, really strong when it comes</text><text start="5077.12" dur="4.4">to MAGA GOP and Republicans holding on</text><text start="5079.679" dur="3.761">to that vote.</text><text start="5081.52" dur="4.4">This one, okay, the president</text><text start="5083.44" dur="4.799">Republicans most admire, it&amp;#39;s Donald</text><text start="5085.92" dur="5.279">Trump. This is a historic comparison. A</text><text start="5088.239" dur="4.321">majority of Republicans say 53% say he&amp;#39;s</text><text start="5091.199" dur="3.44">the Republican president they most</text><text start="5092.56" dur="4.4">admire. Ronald Reagan who traditionally</text><text start="5094.639" dur="5.361">has won that match. Donald Trump nearly</text><text start="5096.96" dur="5.6">triples up on this. Reagan at just 18%.</text><text start="5100" dur="4.08">And then Abraham Lincoln who by most</text><text start="5102.56" dur="3.92">historic accounts is the greatest</text><text start="5104.08" dur="4.079">president of all time. But Republicans</text><text start="5106.48" dur="4.48">say that the president that they most</text><text start="5108.159" dur="5.921">admire by what is this is this six seven</text><text start="5110.96" dur="4.64">times as many. Donald John Trump at 53%</text><text start="5114.08" dur="3.44">easily crushing Abe Lincoln Blinkin at</text><text start="5115.6" dur="3.36">8%. And the Elon poll showed that he was</text><text start="5117.52" dur="2.719">the greatest president as well. Donald</text><text start="5118.96" dur="2.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; feel like this slide might end up on a</text><text start="5120.239" dur="2.721">print out on his desk.</text><text start="5121.6" dur="5.36">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you.</text><text start="5122.96" dur="7.04">What an honor that is. Thank you, CNN.</text><text start="5126.96" dur="5.279">So, in conclusion, if you elect a</text><text start="5130" dur="5.28">Republican House and a Republican Senate</text><text start="5132.239" dur="8.681">on November 3rd, we will continue to put</text><text start="5135.28" dur="5.64">America first every single day.</text><text start="5142.719" dur="5.841">We will win the war on corruption and</text><text start="5145.199" dur="5.201">fraud led by our great vice president J.</text><text start="5148.56" dur="4.4">D. Van. You happen to know him. He comes</text><text start="5150.4" dur="5.759">from these parts.</text><text start="5152.96" dur="5.679">He loves He loves your state. We will</text><text start="5156.159" dur="4.961">pass the No Invasion of our Country Act,</text><text start="5158.639" dur="5.121">prohibiting any future president from</text><text start="5161.12" dur="6.64">ever opening our borders to illegal</text><text start="5163.76" dur="6.479">immigrants again.</text><text start="5167.76" dur="4.56">We will ban sanctuary cities and pass</text><text start="5170.239" dur="4.881">the death penalty for large-scale drug</text><text start="5172.32" dur="5.839">dealers, human traffickers, and anyone</text><text start="5175.12" dur="7.079">who kills a police officer or a member</text><text start="5178.159" dur="4.04">of law enforcement.</text><text start="5183.28" dur="6.64">We will pass voter identification, proof</text><text start="5186.88" dur="6.319">of citizenship, and the Save America Act</text><text start="5189.92" dur="5.759">to defend our sacred American elections.</text><text start="5193.199" dur="5.52">We will save them.</text><text start="5195.679" dur="6.161">Made a lot of progress.</text><text start="5198.719" dur="6.401">And we will enshrine in permanent law no</text><text start="5201.84" dur="7.72">men in women&amp;#39;s sports and no transgender</text><text start="5205.12" dur="4.44">mutilization of your children.</text><text start="5211.679" dur="5.52">So ladies and gentlemen of Ohio, it&amp;#39;s an</text><text start="5214.32" dur="5.28">honor to be with you. The golden age of</text><text start="5217.199" dur="4.401">America is upon us, but you must get out</text><text start="5219.6" dur="5.599">and vote. You have to vote Republican</text><text start="5221.6" dur="9.599">and vote for John Houston and Vake</text><text start="5225.199" dur="7.44">Ramiswami. Two great people</text><text start="5231.199" dur="3.04">be very proud of that vote. You&amp;#39;re going</text><text start="5232.639" dur="4.56">to look back and you&amp;#39;re going to be very</text><text start="5234.239" dur="5.041">proud of those votes. Early voting ends</text><text start="5237.199" dur="3.921">this Sunday, November 1st. Go out and</text><text start="5239.28" dur="4.399">vote as soon as possible. You know what</text><text start="5241.12" dur="4.88">you have to do? November November 3rd,</text><text start="5243.679" dur="5.281">you go out and vote. We&amp;#39;ve already made</text><text start="5246" dur="5.199">unbelievable progress. And now we will</text><text start="5248.96" dur="4.16">reach new levels of greatness, greatness</text><text start="5251.199" dur="4.241">that nobody thought even possible. We&amp;#39;re</text><text start="5253.12" dur="4.079">already there, but I&amp;#39;m talking about</text><text start="5255.44" dur="4.64">greatness that nobody thought would even</text><text start="5257.199" dur="4.881">be possible for a country. It&amp;#39;s my honor</text><text start="5260.08" dur="3.68">to be your president during such an</text><text start="5262.08" dur="2.8">exciting time in the life of our</text><text start="5263.76" dur="2.959">country.</text><text start="5264.88" dur="4.24">We&amp;#39;ve been doing this for 11 years</text><text start="5266.719" dur="4.401">together and there&amp;#39;s never been anything</text><text start="5269.12" dur="5.64">like it and there probably never will be</text><text start="5271.12" dur="3.64">anything like it.</text><text start="5276.4" dur="5.52">So let&amp;#39;s get out and do what we do best,</text><text start="5279.36" dur="5.92">which is to win. We know how to win. So</text><text start="5281.92" dur="5.12">on November 3rd, go out, vote properly.</text><text start="5285.28" dur="3.04">We&amp;#39;re going to win like nobody&amp;#39;s ever</text><text start="5287.04" dur="4.8">seen before.</text><text start="5288.32" dur="6">Let&amp;#39;s make the next two years bigger,</text><text start="5291.84" dur="4.56">better, and stronger than ever before.</text><text start="5294.32" dur="5.839">Because together,</text><text start="5296.4" dur="7.36">we will make America powerful again,</text><text start="5300.159" dur="8.401">wealthy again, healthy again, STRONG</text><text start="5303.76" dur="8.16">AGAIN, PROUD AGAIN, SAFE AGAIN,</text><text start="5308.56" dur="7.119">and most importantly, we will make</text><text start="5311.92" dur="6.319">America great again. Thank you, Ohio.</text><text start="5315.679" dur="2.56">Thank you.</text></transcript>